comes back with a wrench. “Leave it here,” I say, though the door stays loose. “It came back with a loose screw.” The wrench taps against my palm."}, {"id": "R009", "text": "i leave the familiar routine with one misplaced item and mark the halfway point. i put it on the bench, then turn it by hand. if it still moves, i keep the original and leave the neighbor’s note."}, {"id": "R010", "text": "i put the old item back and mark the halfway point. “i’ll leave it, then i’ll try the next one.” i leave the new one in the drawer. “i’ll stop when the old one goes.” i mark the halfway point again. “i’ll keep the old one if i get a bad result.” i leave the old item in the drawer. “i’ll call that a trial.”"}, {"id": "R011", "text": "i put the old tin tin beside the shelf and check the shelf again. i leave the tin beside it for a moment, then set it beside the bench. \"i will check the old tin again,\" i say, and i set it beside the old tin."}, {"id": "R012", "text": "left. the wrench taps my thigh. i follow the sound with the rag. the item stays. i turn the rag over, then the needle. the needle ticks. i leave the item and the rag. the needle stays. the routine starts again."}]
